SUMMARY
Explicitly an APT hunt scenario. Hunters must apply threat intelligence to guide their search, identify APT TTPs in log data, and trace a full campaign — directly matching the 'intel-led hunting' approach used in mature hunt programmes.

LEARNING OBJECTIVES
- Start investigations from security alerts on quarantined files"
- Identify phishing emails impersonating trusted partners using reply-to manipulation
- Decode base64-encoded PowerShell commands to understand attacker actions
- Trace malware from initial file creation through process execution to C2 communication
- Recognize watering hole attacks through outbound browsing patterns"
- Identify credential theft tools and lateral movement"
- Analyze authentication logs for external attacker logins"
- Map attacker infrastructure using PassiveDNS pivoting"
- Attribute attacks to known APT groups using public threat intelligence"
- Identify data exfiltration using rclone and mailbox export"

